From 08c2d8f85dc2cf557fedcb7e11ba9f1d878bd1c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 12:45:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/52] ARA environment adaptations: AraSDR/AraRACH RF/TDD
 support

Faithful capture of the uncommitted working-tree changes on the ARA gNB
container (kaiair-bs-1) atop upstream ocudu dev @ 67dab6bc. Enables the
USRP X310 TDD deployment used by the ARA testbed:
  - lower-PHY discontinuous-TX burst gating (drop UL/special slots; cut
    partial DL slots at the last active symbol)
  - X3x0/X410/N3x0 FP0 GPIO ATR gating of the external PA/RF switch in
    sync with the TDD pattern (without it the radio does not transmit)
  - RU SDR config plumbing of the TDD pattern + lower-PHY test coverage

Captured by KaiAir; original work by the AraSDR/AraRACH effort.

Co-authored-by: AraSDR/AraRACH <arawireless@iastate.edu>
